**Troy Goode owns the most code that is still here, with about 39% of the surviving lines. Douglas Christopher Wilson is second with 33.1%.** Troy's figure counts two addresses as one person, which is a guess (details below).

I counted lines with `git blame -w -M -C` at HEAD. That is the default copy detection setting, and the copy-detection note named no one as shifting by more than 2 points. The count covers 19 files and 1,664 non-blank lines (1,997 with blank lines).

| Author | Lines (non-blank) | Share | With blank lines | Commits (share) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Troy Goode (2 addresses, merged)** | 649 | 39.0% | 810 (40.8%) | 95 (30.1%) |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 551 | 33.1% | 629 (31.7%) | 143 (45.3%) |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 80 | 4.8% | 95 (4.8%) | 2 (0.6%) |
| Jon Church | 59 | 3.5% | 72 (3.6%) | 3 (0.9%) |
| Sebastian Beltran | 57 | 3.4% | 67 (3.4%) | 2 (0.6%) |
| Ulises Gascón | 46 | 2.8% | 52 (2.6%) | 3 (0.9%) |
| Ignacio Mangas | 38 | 2.3% | 44 (2.2%) | 2 (0.6%) |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 30 | 1.8% | 34 (1.7%) | 5 (1.6%) |
| Linus Unnebäck | 26 | 1.6% | 26 (1.3%) | 1 (0.3%) |
| Ollie Buck | 14 | 0.8% | 17 (0.9%) | 1 (0.3%) |

52 more authors hold 6.9% together. The largest of them is Eric di Domenico at 0.7%.

**Commits are misleading here.** Douglas has the most commits (143, 45.3%) but fewer surviving lines than Troy, who has 95 commits.

**Identities**
- **Troy Goode:** he appears under `<email redacted>` (605 lines, 36.4%, 93 commits) and `troy@laptop.example` (44 lines, 2.6%, 2 commits). The tool rates this link as strong evidence, but it is a guess from names and addresses until you confirm it. Unmerged, Troy is still first at 36.4%, ahead of Douglas at 33.1%. Nothing was written to `.mailmap`, so merging is in memory only.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades:** the same address, `<email redacted>`, also appears under the name `alex94puchades`. The tool counted both names as one person, so his 30 lines include both.

**Left out**
- **Reformat commit:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", by Fiona Formatter) is ignored through `.git-blame-ignore-revs`. It rewrote 1,016 lines across `lib/index.js` and 3 test files. Without the ignore, Fiona would hold those lines instead of their earlier authors.
- **Bot:** `dependabot[bot]` is excluded, with 10 lines and 11 commits. Those lines are not credited to anyone.

**Mechanical rewrites:** the tool checked 141 commits that still hold surviving lines. It set none aside automatically, and it counted `62628c0` as the one ignored by the ignore file. Five more look mechanical, and I kept all five in the counts. I did not inspect any of them except `fcd2b56`, which touches 10 files with an ESLint cleanup.
- `739dc11` "docs: reformat license" (Douglas, 17 lines)
- `fcd2b56` "switch to ESLint; clean up" (Troy, 14 lines)
- `00d6eec` "build: use yaml eslint configuration" (Douglas, 9 lines)
- `344ce1e` "build: <email redacted>" (Douglas, 1 line)
- `9c2b59d` "build: <email redacted>" (Douglas, 1 line)

**Bus factor**
- **Two authors:** Troy (merged) and Douglas together hold 72.1% of the whole repo's non-blank lines (72.4% with blank lines). The bus factor is the fewest authors whose surviving lines reach 50%. Unmerged, the same two hold 69.5%.
- **To reach 80%:** 4 authors if Troy is merged, 5 if not. Both numbers are for the whole repo.

**Activity**
- **Troy's main address:** his last commit under `<email redacted>` was 2019-05-27.
- **Douglas:** his last commit was 2021-09-07.
- **Recent authors:** several smaller holders committed in 2025–2026, including Jon Church, Ulises Gascón and Ignacio Mangas.

Surviving lines show whose code is still here. They don't show code quality, review work or design work, and code deleted on purpose counts for nobody.

