 - Bash: for a in "Troy Goode" "Douglas Christopher Wilson" "Íñigo Marquínez Prado" "Jon Church" "Sebastian Beltran" "Ulises Gascón"; do echo "$a: $(git log --author="$a" --format=%ad --date=short -1)"; done; git ls-files | xargs wc -l | sort -rn | head -8
FINAL ANSWER:
Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson own about 73% of the surviving lines. I used `git blame` on `HEAD` rather than the busfactor skill, because the skill weights commits by recency instead of counting the lines that remain.

Per-file blame used `-w -M -C`. It also used `--ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs`, so the 4-space/double-quote reformat commit (`62628c0`) doesn't count as ownership. The repo has 19 tracked files and 1,995 lines in total.

| Author | Surviving lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 810 | ~41% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | ~32% |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | ~5% |
| Jon Church | 72 | ~4% |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | ~3% |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | ~3% |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 | ~2% |
